quran[9]{c,v,t}:
  10,62,"Beware! Indeed, the close friends of Allah shall have no fear on them, nor shall they grieve."
  10,63,(They are) those who are (true) believers and are God-conscious.
  10,64,There are glad tidings for them in this worldly life and the Hereafter. There is no change to the Words of Allah. That is the supreme success.
  10,65,"Do not let their (malicious) words grieve you. Indeed, honour belongs to Allah entirely. He is the All-Hearing, the All-Knowing."
  10,66,"Beware! Indeed, to Allah belongs whoever is in the heavens and whoever is on the earth. Those who worship partner gods besides Allah do not (actually) follow them; they follow nothing but assumptions. And they are just telling lies."
  10,67,He is the One Who made the night for you so that you might rest in it and the day (bright) to see. There are signs in it for people who listen.
  10,68,They say: ‘Allah has taken a son (for Himself)!’ Glory be to Him. He is the Self-Sufficient. To Him belongs whatever is in the heavens and whatever is on the earth. You have no authority to say this. Do you attribute to Allah what you do not know?
  10,69,"Say: ‘Surely, those who fabricate lies against Allah shall not prosper.’"
  10,70,"There is an enjoyment (for a few days) in this world, then to Us shall be their return. And We shall make them taste severe punishment for their having disbelieved."
